00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
Speaker 1: One of the things I think is really&nbsp;
important for all of us to be able to do is to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.540
figure out when we see a headline, when we&nbsp;
start seeing something, enter the discussion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:15.660
and get repeated over and over again. And it's a&nbsp;
major claim. We need to be able to figure out for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:23.220
ourselves, is it backed by evidence or is this&nbsp;
disinformation or misinformation? And we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:29.160
the perfect example today. There is a new I'm&nbsp;
going to use some of the words they're using,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:38.160
even though they're B.S., quite frankly. There&nbsp;
is a new, quote, study about COVID vaccines from,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:45.780
quote, Florida floating around, which I started&nbsp;
seeing over the weekend during my live streams. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:52.020
saw some of the people in the chat saying, David.&nbsp;
New study from Florida says that COVID vaccines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:59.040
increase heart attacks by 84% in the month&nbsp;
after one is vaccinated. When you get a vaccine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:07.080
your odds of a heart attack go up 84% for&nbsp;
the month after you've received that vaccine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:13.080
So the first question with all of these things&nbsp;
is, does it pass the sniff test? So with some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:18.600
of these things, you know, it turns out we&nbsp;
don't breathe oxygen. We actually breathe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:26.160
really light water, you know, so I don't know. We&nbsp;
would say this doesn't even pass the sniff test.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.260
It's not really even worth looking into. Now,&nbsp;
let's imagine it were true that getting a COVID&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:37.860
vaccine increases your chances of a heart attack&nbsp;
by 84%. We would be talking about so many heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:45.000
attacks, heart attacks and deaths that we would&nbsp;
have heard about this more so more quickly than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.000
two years into vaccination. But let's imagine&nbsp;
that we want to take this seriously and explore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:59.040
it. The source of this is Florida's surgeon&nbsp;
general, Joseph Ladapo, a known anti-vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:06.060
voice. And Ars Technica has a really good write&nbsp;
up about this so-called analysis. And he put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:14.820
out a statement on Friday that men age 18 to 39&nbsp;
should not get the COVID vaccine. Why not? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:22.440
he claims to have an analysis called exploring the&nbsp;
relationship between all cause and cardiac related&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:30.420
mortality following COVID 19 vaccination or&nbsp;
infection in Florida Residents A Self-controlled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:37.200
Case Series Study. There is then a press release&nbsp;
about the analysis, so now we're like a layer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.420
removed. Now it's a press release about an&nbsp;
analysis. The press release says COVID vaccines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:50.460
cause an 84% increase in the relative incidence&nbsp;
of cardiac related death among males 18 to 39&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:58.380
within 28 days following marina vaccination.&nbsp;
There's a lot of important data in that claim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:05.100
or important metrics in that claim which we are&nbsp;
going to look at. So let's take a look at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:10.320
analysis. One of the things you might notice when&nbsp;
you pull up the analysis is it's supposedly from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:15.720
