has the vaccine, the other doesn't. And they are&nbsp;
otherwise identical groups in a self-controlled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:38.160
case series, which is what was done. There's no&nbsp;
control group. The only people in their study&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:47.040
are the people that are being studied and whose&nbsp;
outcomes are being measured. There's no control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:53.340
group. It's, you know, got a COVID vaccine died&nbsp;
within 25 weeks. And then they look subsequently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:58.140
at the group that died within the first four&nbsp;
weeks. And what they wanted to see was, are the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:03.060
deaths clustered in the first four weeks after&nbsp;
the vaccination, which is considered the risk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:08.580
period for a vaccine during which a side effect or&nbsp;
